@startuml
title Bulk Import Word CSV Sequence (/vocabulary/import and /api/admin/words/import)

autonumber
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor Admin
boundary "Bulk Import Word CSV UI" as ImportUi
control "VocabularyController\n(FE Dashboard)" as FeController
control "AdminWordsController\n(BE API)" as BeController
entity "BulkImportResult\n(FE Response DTO)" as FeBulkImportDto
entity "ImportWordsRequest\n(BE Request DTO)" as BeImportRequestDto
entity "BulkImportResponse\n(BE Response DTO)" as BeBulkImportDto
entity "BulkImportErrorResponse\n(BE Response DTO)" as BeBulkImportErrorDto
control "WordAdminService" as WordService
entity "Word" as WordEntity
entity "WordSense" as WordSenseEntity
entity "WordExample" as WordExampleEntity
entity "Topic" as TopicEntity
entity "WordTopic" as WordTopicEntity
control "WordAdminRepository" as WordRepository
database "VocaNovaDbContext" as DbContext
database "MySQL Database" as MySQL

note over ImportUi, MySQL
Checked in current code:
Dashboard UI file exists: Views/Vocabulary/Import.cshtml.
FE controller exists: VocabularyController.
FE response DTO exists: BulkImportResult with BulkImportError.
BE controller exists: AdminWordsController.
BE DTOs exist: ImportWordsRequest, BulkImportResponse and BulkImportErrorResponse.
Endpoint is POST /api/admin/words/import with multipart CSV file.
Entities exist: Word, WordSense, WordExample, Topic and WordTopic.
end note

Admin -> ImportUi: Choose CSV file
Admin -> ImportUi: Upload CSV
ImportUi -> FeController: POST /vocabulary/import\nIFormFile
FeController -> FeController: Validate file exists

alt No CSV selected
    FeController --> ImportUi: Return JSON error
else CSV selected
    FeController -> BeController: VocaNovaApiClient.ImportWordsAsync\nPOST /api/admin/words/import
    BeController -> BeImportRequestDto: Bind multipart form
    BeImportRequestDto --> BeController: ImportWordsRequest
    BeController -> BeController: Check admin authorization
    BeController -> WordService: ImportCsvAsync(uploaded content)
    WordService -> WordService: Validate CSV file,\nheader and rows

    alt CSV invalid
        WordService --> BeController: Validation failure
        BeController --> FeController: HTTP 400 error
        FeController --> ImportUi: Show import error
    else CSV valid
        loop For each CSV row
            WordService -> WordRepository: Find or create word data
            WordRepository -> DbContext: Query existing word\nand topics
            DbContext -> MySQL: SELECT words,\nSELECT topics
            MySQL --> DbContext: Existing rows
            DbContext -> WordEntity: Read or create Word
            DbContext -> TopicEntity: Read Topic rows
            WordEntity --> DbContext: Word data
            TopicEntity --> DbContext: Topic data
            WordRepository -> WordSenseEntity: Create or update WordSense
            WordRepository -> WordExampleEntity: Create WordExample?
            WordRepository -> WordTopicEntity: Create WordTopic links?
            WordSenseEntity --> WordRepository: WordSense
            WordExampleEntity --> WordRepository: WordExample?
            WordTopicEntity --> WordRepository: WordTopic links?
            WordRepository -> DbContext: Save imported row
            DbContext -> MySQL: INSERT/UPDATE words,\nword_senses, word_examples,\nword_topics
            MySQL --> DbContext: Save result
            DbContext --> WordRepository: Row result
            WordRepository --> WordService: Imported or skipped row
        end

        WordService --> BeController: Bulk import result
        BeController -> BeBulkImportDto: Create BulkImportResponse
        BeController -> BeBulkImportErrorDto: Create error list
        BeBulkImportErrorDto --> BeBulkImportDto: Errors
        BeBulkImportDto --> BeController: BulkImportResponse
        BeController -> FeBulkImportDto: HTTP 200 OK\nBulkImportResponse JSON
        FeBulkImportDto --> FeController: BulkImportResult
        FeController --> ImportUi: Show imported/skipped/errors
    end
end

@enduml
